      "slug": "alternate-nostril",
      "name": "Alternate-Nostril Breathing",
      "summary": "Thumb closes the right nostril, ring finger the left. In through the left, out through the right, in through the right, out through the left — that sequence is one cycle, and the four beats on screen are its four breaths in order. A traditional practice with modest trial support and an unmistakable knack for holding attention.",
